{
 "brief": "A crisis expert warned the Peace Council that temporary truces in Gaza risk becoming permanent drains on resources and humanitarian capacity, Shehab Wire reported. He criticized the council for equating aggressor and victim, calling such framing a false equivalence that obscures the conflict's fundamentals.\n\nThe expert demanded an international monitoring mechanism capable of ending the crisis rather than merely administering it. He rejected approaches treating the Gaza situation as a manageable problem requiring ongoing oversight, insisting instead on measures aimed at resolving the underlying conflict.",
